course: dictionary
lesson: 15024
title: A respondent answers
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A respondent is a person who answers. When someone asks a survey, a questionnaire or a question, the people who give the answers are the respondents. Each child who fills in a class survey about favourite sports is a respondent.
explain: «Twenty respondents chose pizza as their favourite food.» Here the word counts the people who answered the survey. Each of those twenty people gave an answer, so each one is a respondent.
explain: The word is also used in law. «The respondent had to answer the claim in court.» In a court case, the respondent is the person who must reply to what the other side says. Check by putting "person who answers" into the sentence: if it still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: A respondent is a person who answers a survey, a questionnaire or a question.
fact: «Respondents» is the plural, meaning more than one person who answers.
fact: In maths, a survey can count respondents, as in «20 respondents chose pizza».
fact: In law, the respondent is the person who must answer a case in court, for example in a divorce or an appeal.
fact: The majority of respondents means most of the people who answered.
exercise: «Twenty respondents chose pizza as their favourite food.» What is a respondent? | *A person who answers a survey or question | A teacher who writes the survey | A person who cooks the food | A pizza topping
exercise: «Each respondent filled in the form in five minutes.» What did each respondent do? | Went home early | Sang a song | *Filled in the form | Cooked a meal
exercise: In a court case, what must the respondent do? | Ring the bell to start | *Answer the claim made against them | Give a prize to the winner | Judge the case
test: Mia asks, «How many respondents took part in our survey?» What does respondents mean here? | Shopkeepers | Sports players | *People who answered the survey | Scientists
test: Which word is the plural of respondent? | Responder | Respond | *Respondents | Responsive
exam: Which sentence uses respondent correctly? | The respondent sang loudly in the playground. | *Ten respondents filled in our survey about school lunches. | The respondent ate her lunch under the big tree. | Respondent is a big red dog.
